# Cloudflare *appends* every matching rule rather than letting the most
# specific one win, so `/*` must not set Cache-Control — see the landing's
# copy of this file. The SPA shell keeps the platform default
# (public, max-age=0, must-revalidate), which is exactly right: a cached shell
# that outlived its asset hashes is a blank page.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Vite fingerprints these.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
